    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "4. The prosecution allegations in brief are that the informant-Raj Kishore Mishra had come into contact with accused Sanjay Kumar Nayak and his wife-accused Dipalika Mohanty 2-3 years back.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2194,
      "end": 2383,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Raj Kishore Mishra",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 2257,
          "end": 2275
        },
        {
          "text": "Sanjay Kumar Nayak",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 2311,
          "end": 2329
        },
        {
          "text": "Dipalika Mohanty",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 2351,
          "end": 2367
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.18596957623958588
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 17,
      "text": "They introduced themselves as employees of Orissa Thermal Power Plant Corporation (in short \"OTPCL\") and stated that they could arrange jobs for the relatives of the informant in OTPCL and also engage the JCB machine of his brother Raj Ratan Mishra in OTPCL.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2384,
      "end": 2643,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Orissa Thermal Power Plant Corporation",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 2428,
          "end": 2466
        },
        {
          "text": "OTPCL",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 2564,
          "end": 2569
        },
        {
          "text": "Raj Ratan Mishra",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 2617,
          "end": 2633
        },
        {
          "text": "OTPCL",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 2637,
          "end": 2642
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.16530074179172516
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "For this purpose, Sanjay Kumar Nayak had taken Rs.53,00,000/- from the petitioner.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2644,
      "end": 2726,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sanjay Kumar Nayak",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 2662,
          "end": 2680
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.197597473859787
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "Rs.10,00,000/- through bank transaction and Rs.43,00,000/- through cash paid to him, Dipalika Mohanty and his son Vishal Nayak.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2727,
      "end": 2854,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Dipalika Mohanty",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 2812,
          "end": 2828
        },
        {
          "text": "Vishal Nayak",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 2841,
          "end": 2853
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.20940302312374115
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 20,
      "text": "When after one year, no appointment letter was received and the informant found that Sanjay Kumar Nayak and Dipalika Mohanty had switched off their phones, he lodged F.I.R. and the case was registered against the petitioners on 06.05.2023 under Section 419/420 of IPC.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2855,
      "end": 3123,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sanjay Kumar Nayak",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 2940,
          "end": 2958
        },
        {
          "text": "Dipalika Mohanty",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 2963,
          "end": 2979
        },
        {
          "text": "06.05.2023",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 3083,
          "end": 3093
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 419/420",
